## The plugin's bin/ ships the launcher script and its release checksum —
## source, not build output — so un-ignore those specific files despite the
## blanket "bin/" rule above. This is an explicit allow-list, not just an
## unignore of the two files: `!/plugins/**/bin/` only makes the directory
## traversable again, so contents are re-ignored by `/plugins/**/bin/*`
## (covering both loose files and the whole bin/server/ subdirectory, which
## the published server build — fetched from a GitHub Release at runtime, see
## bin/server.js — must stay part of; a local `dotnet publish -o .../bin` for
## testing should never be committed again) before the two specific files
## needed are un-ignored again.
!/plugins/**/bin/
/plugins/**/bin/*
!/plugins/**/bin/server.js
!/plugins/**/bin/*.sha256
